TEST DATA AND DEVELOPMENT TOOLS (NOT IN THE EXECUTABLE)
=======================================================

Test recordings (e2e/testdata/audio/)
  Staged recordings made for this repository: an invented oral-history
  interview and a short note, spoken by the Piper voices "kerstin" (low)
  and "thorsten" (high) and laid out by e2e/make-audio.py. No real person
  is recorded. The recordings and the prepared results beside them are
  covered by the MPL like the rest of the repository.
  The voices: https://huggingface.co/rhasspy/piper-voices, MIT License
  (Rhasspy, Michael Hansen); thorsten also published by its speaker under
  the MIT License, https://huggingface.co/Thorsten-Voice/Piper. Trained on
  the datasets Thorsten-Voice (Thorsten Mueller) and kerstin
  (https://github.com/rhasspy/dataset-voice-kerstin), both CC0 1.0.

OCR test set (testdata/ocr/)
  The same three images as Moliri's server/transcribe/testdata/ocr. The index
  card and the object label are synthetic, generated for Moliri; they are
  covered by the MPL like the rest of the repository. The Fraktur page is page
  XV of the preface of the Grimms' "Kinder- und Haus-Maerchen", vol. 1, 1857,
  a Google Books scan in the public domain, from Wikimedia Commons
  (File:Kinder_und_Hausmärchen_(Grimm)_1857_I_p_015.jpg). Its ground truth
  (fraktur.gt.txt) is the proofread transcription of de.wikisource, Creative
  Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 (CC BY-SA 4.0),
  https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/; it is not covered by the
  MPL. Source, authors and changes: testdata/ocr/fraktur.gt.txt.license.

